IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`
IMPORT domain

-- g1-adverse-action.l4: s.10 of the Regulation of Engagement in Work on Refrigeration or Air-Conditioning Systems Law
-- 5785-2025 (Sefer HaChukim 3349 pp. 184-185), refusal to renew a licence, its revocation, restriction or suspension.
-- Group G1.  Imports prelude, daydate, il-interpretation-time and domain.  The Hebrew is copied by script from
-- inputs/law.wiki (src:N is line N); identifiers and glosses are mine and the Hebrew governs.  "IL s.10(c)" is the
-- Interpretation Law's rule on days of rest; "s.10(c)" alone is this Law's cure power.
--
-- What is an input here: the six grounds (facts the caller supplies), the Registrar's opinions (that a defect can be
-- cured, that the gravity of the matter or the public interest requires a suspension, that an offence makes the
-- licensee unfit, that a defect was cured to his satisfaction), the Council's consultation (IP7) and the written
-- hearing, the length of any period the Registrar fixes.  None gets a default.
-- Periods met here, each with its fork in FRAGMENT-G1.md:
--   P10  a restriction or suspension of at most three years (kind V, a period of validity): IL s.10(c) not applied;
--   P11  a suspension until final judgment (kind V): no end and no number, NOTHING;
--   P12  the period the Registrar sets for a cure (kind D, a deadline for doing something): IL s.10(c) applied;
--   P13  the period after a revocation before a new application may be made (kind W, a window for an application):
--        IL s.10(c) applied.
-- The alternative of each is a callable function with a test.

§ `Chapter 2: Licensing (continued)`

§§ `s.10 Refusal to renew, revocation, restriction or suspension`

-- The measures of s.10(a).
@desc The five measures section 10(a) lets the Registrar take against a licence: refuse its renewal, condition its renewal on a training course under section 17, revoke it, restrict it, suspend it
DECLARE `Measure under section 10(a)` IS ONE OF
    `refuse to renew the licence`
    `make the renewal of the licence conditional on taking part in a training course under section 17`
    `revoke the licence`
    `restrict the licence`
    `suspend the licence`

@desc The acts of the Registrar under section 10: the measures of (a), the suspension of (b), the direction of (c), and the direction and conditions of (d)
DECLARE `Act of the Registrar under section 10` IS ONE OF
    `take a measure against a licence under section 10(a)` HAS `the measure` IS A `Measure under section 10(a)`
    `suspend a licence until final judgment`
    `direct a licensee not to do specified work until a curable defect is cured`
    `fix the period before a new application may be made after a revocation`
    `add conditions to the grant of a new licence`

-- What is missing when the Registrar may not take a measure.  The list is empty when he may.
@desc A precondition of a power of the Registrar under section 10 that is not met; a power exists when the list of unmet preconditions is empty
DECLARE `Unmet precondition of section 10` IS ONE OF
    `no ground of section 10(a) is made out`
    `the Council was not consulted under section 10`
    `the Council's advice was not validly given under section 10`
    `the licensee was not given an opportunity to make claims in writing`
    `the restriction or suspension has no period fixed`
    `the restriction or suspension runs beyond the three years section 10(a) allows`
    `no indictment was filed for an offence as stated in section 6(a)(3)`
    `the Registrar did not find that the gravity of the matter or the public interest requires the suspension`
    `the Registrar does not hold that the defect can be cured`
    `the defect was cured to the satisfaction of the Registrar, so the second limb does not arise`
    `the period the Registrar set has not yet passed`
    `the licence was not revoked under section 10(a)`

@ref s.10 (src:110)
GIVEN condition IS A BOOLEAN
      item IS AN `Unmet precondition of section 10`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Unmet precondition of section 10`
`the unmet precondition of section 10 listed when` condition item MEANS
    IF condition THEN LIST item ELSE EMPTY

§§ `s.10(a) The six grounds and the measures`

-- (a): "The Registrar may, after consulting the Council, refuse to renew a licence, make its renewal conditional
-- on taking part in a training course as stated in s.17, revoke a licence, restrict it or suspend it for a
-- period not exceeding three years, after giving the licensee an opportunity to make his claims in writing, where
-- one of these holds:" and the six grounds.
-- src:110 | {{ח:תת|(א)}} הרשם רשאי, לאחר התייעצות עם המועצה, לסרב לחדש רישיון, להתנות את חידוש הרישיון בהשתתפות בהשתלמות כאמור {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 17|בסעיף 17}}, לבטל רישיון, להגבילו או להתלותו לתקופה שלא תעלה על שלוש שנים, לאחר שנתן לבעל הרישיון הזדמנות לטעון את טענותיו בכתב, בהתקיים אחד מאלה:
-- src:111 | {{ח:תתת|(1)}} הרישיון ניתן על יסוד מידע כוזב, שגוי, מטעה או חלקי;
-- src:112 | {{ח:תתת|(2)}} חדל להתקיים תנאי מהתנאים למתן הרישיון לפי {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 6|סעיפים 6}} {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 9|או 9}}, לפי העניין;
-- src:113 | {{ח:תתת|(3)}} בעל הרישיון הפר תנאי מתנאי הרישיון;
-- src:114 | {{ח:תתת|(4)}} בעל הרישיון הפר חובה או איסור שהוטלו עליו לפי חוק זה או שהוטלו עליו לפי חיקוק אחר בקשר עם פעילותו כבעל רישיון;
-- src:115 | {{ח:תתת|(5)}} בעל הרישיון מסר לרשם, לעובד אחר של המשרד או למפקח שדרש ממנו מידע לשם מילוי תפקידו, מידע כוזב, מטעה, שגוי או חלקי בקשר לפעילותו כבעל רישיון;
-- src:116 | {{ח:תתת|(6)}} בעל הרישיון גילה חוסר מקצועיות או רשלנות שעלולים לגרום לסיכון חיי אדם או לנזק לרכוש, במסגרת פעילותו כבעל רישיון.
@ref s.10(a) (src:110-116)
@desc The six grounds of section 10(a): each is a fact the caller supplies
DECLARE `Grounds under section 10(a)` HAS
    `the licence was granted on false, mistaken, misleading or partial information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Ground (1): True if the licence was granted on the basis of information that was false, mistaken, misleading or partial
    `a condition for the grant ceased to hold` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Ground (2): True if a condition for the grant of the licence under section 6 or section 9 ceased to hold; the conditions of the licence still hold is G2's rule (IP18)
    `the only condition that ceased to hold is a condition of section 6(a)(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the only condition that ceased to hold is the training or qualification condition of section 6(a)(4), which section 8 leaves out of a renewal; read only by the reading that carries section 8 into this ground
    `the licensee breached a licence condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Ground (3): True if the licensee breached a condition of the licence, the section 17 training duty included (IP8)
    `the licensee breached a duty or prohibition under the Law or another enactment in connection with the activity as a licensee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Ground (4): True if the licensee breached a duty or prohibition imposed on them under the Law, or under another enactment in connection with their activity as a licensee
    `the licensee gave false, misleading, mistaken or partial information when it was demanded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Ground (5): True if the licensee gave the Registrar, another employee of the Ministry or an inspector who demanded information in order to perform their function, information that was false, misleading, mistaken or partial, in connection with their activity as a licensee
    `the licensee showed lack of professionalism or negligence that may endanger life or damage property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Ground (6): True if, in their activity as a licensee, the licensee showed lack of professionalism or negligence that may cause a risk to human life or damage to property

@ref s.10(a)(1)-(6) (src:111-116)
GIVEN grounds IS A `Grounds under section 10(a)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a ground of section 10(a) is made out` grounds MEANS
        grounds's `the licence was granted on false, mistaken, misleading or partial information`
    OR  grounds's `a condition for the grant ceased to hold`
    OR  grounds's `the licensee breached a licence condition`
    OR  grounds's `the licensee breached a duty or prohibition under the Law or another enactment in connection with the activity as a licensee`
    OR  grounds's `the licensee gave false, misleading, mistaken or partial information when it was demanded`
    OR  grounds's `the licensee showed lack of professionalism or negligence that may endanger life or damage property`

-- The same grounds on the reading that carries s.8 into ground (2): a renewal does not require the s.6(a)(4)
-- condition (s.8), so the loss of that condition alone cannot ground a REFUSAL TO RENEW.  Every other measure reads
-- the grounds as above.
@ref s.10(a)(2) (src:112); s.8
GIVEN grounds IS A `Grounds under section 10(a)`
      measure IS A `Measure under section 10(a)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a ground of section 10(a) is made out for the measure, the renewal conditions of section 8 carried into ground (2)` grounds measure MEANS
    IF       measure EQUALS `refuse to renew the licence`
         AND grounds's `the only condition that ceased to hold is a condition of section 6(a)(4)`
    THEN     grounds's `the licence was granted on false, mistaken, misleading or partial information`
         OR  grounds's `the licensee breached a licence condition`
         OR  grounds's `the licensee breached a duty or prohibition under the Law or another enactment in connection with the activity as a licensee`
         OR  grounds's `the licensee gave false, misleading, mistaken or partial information when it was demanded`
         OR  grounds's `the licensee showed lack of professionalism or negligence that may endanger life or damage property`
    ELSE `a ground of section 10(a) is made out` grounds

-- The period of a restriction or suspension (P10): its first day and its last day, if one is fixed.
@desc The period of a restriction or suspension: its first day and its last day, if one is fixed
DECLARE `Period of a restriction or suspension under section 10` HAS
    `begins on` IS A DATE @desc The first day of the restriction or suspension
    `ends on` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc The last day of the restriction or suspension; NOTHING if no end is fixed

@ref s.10(a) (src:110)
@desc Everything section 10(a) asks before the Registrar may take a measure against a licence
DECLARE `Circumstances of a measure under section 10(a)` HAS
    `the measure` IS A `Measure under section 10(a)` @desc The measure the Registrar proposes
    `the grounds` IS A `Grounds under section 10(a)` @desc The six grounds, each a fact
    `the Council was consulted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the Registrar consulted the Council before taking the measure (IP7)
    `the Council's advice was validly given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the Council's advice was validly given (quorum, majority, subcommittee delegation: sections 24 to 26) (IP7)
    `the licensee was given an opportunity to make claims in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if, before the measure, the licensee was given the opportunity to make their claims in writing
    `the period of the restriction or suspension` IS A MAYBE `Period of a restriction or suspension under section 10` @desc The period of a restriction or suspension; NOTHING for a measure that has none

-- How the three-year cap of (a) is read.  Taken: the cap reaches a restriction as well as a suspension (the phrase
-- "for a period not exceeding three years" follows "restrict it or suspend it"); the last day allowed is the day
-- IL s.10(b) gives for three years after the day the period begins; IL s.10(c) is not applied (a period of validity).
@desc A reading of the three-year cap of section 10(a): whether the cap counts the day the period begins as its first day, whether it moves past days of rest, and whether it reaches a restriction as well as a suspension
DECLARE `Reading of the three-year cap of section 10(a)` HAS
    `the cap counts the beginning day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the day the period begins is its first day, so that the last day allowed is the day before the third anniversary
    `the cap moves past days of rest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if IL s.10(c) is applied to the end of the cap, so that a cap that falls on a day of rest moves to the next day that is not one
    `the cap reaches restrictions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the cap applies to a restriction as well as to a suspension

@ref s.10(a) (src:110)
`the reading of the cap of section 10(a) taken` MEANS
    `Reading of the three-year cap of section 10(a)` WITH
        `the cap counts the beginning day` IS FALSE
        `the cap moves past days of rest` IS FALSE
        `the cap reaches restrictions` IS TRUE

-- The three readings that depart from the one taken, each a value so that a directive can name it.
@ref s.10(a) (src:110)
`the reading of the cap of section 10(a) moving past days of rest` MEANS
    `Reading of the three-year cap of section 10(a)` WITH
        `the cap counts the beginning day` IS FALSE
        `the cap moves past days of rest` IS TRUE
        `the cap reaches restrictions` IS TRUE

@ref s.10(a) (src:110)
`the reading of the cap of section 10(a) counting the beginning day` MEANS
    `Reading of the three-year cap of section 10(a)` WITH
        `the cap counts the beginning day` IS TRUE
        `the cap moves past days of rest` IS FALSE
        `the cap reaches restrictions` IS TRUE

@ref s.10(a) (src:110)
`the reading of the cap of section 10(a) reaching suspensions only` MEANS
    `Reading of the three-year cap of section 10(a)` WITH
        `the cap counts the beginning day` IS FALSE
        `the cap moves past days of rest` IS FALSE
        `the cap reaches restrictions` IS FALSE

@ref s.10(a) (src:110)
`no days of rest for section 10` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS EMPTY

-- Whether a period that begins on one day and ends on another is within three years.
@ref s.10(a) (src:110)
GIVEN begins IS A DATE
      ends IS A DATE
      reading IS A `Reading of the three-year cap of section 10(a)`
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the period ends within the three-year cap` begins ends reading calendar MEANS
    IF   reading's `the cap counts the beginning day`
    THEN ends LESS THAN (`the last day the cap of section 10(a) allows` begins reading calendar)
    ELSE ends AT MOST (`the last day the cap of section 10(a) allows` begins reading calendar)

@ref s.10(a) (src:110)
GIVEN begins IS A DATE
      reading IS A `Reading of the three-year cap of section 10(a)`
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day the cap of section 10(a) allows` begins reading calendar MEANS
    IF   reading's `the cap moves past days of rest`
    THEN `s 10(b), (c) — the last day of a period of` 3 `years after an event on` begins `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` (`days of rest, recess or holiday listed in` (calendar's `days of rest, recess or holiday`))
    ELSE `s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 3 `years after an event on` begins

-- The unmet preconditions about the period, for a restriction or a suspension.
@ref s.10(a) (src:110)
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstances of a measure under section 10(a)`
      reading IS A `Reading of the three-year cap of section 10(a)`
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Unmet precondition of section 10`
`the unmet preconditions of section 10(a) about the period` c reading calendar MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `the period of the restriction or suspension`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN LIST `the restriction or suspension has no period fixed`
    WHEN JUST period THEN `the unmet preconditions of section 10(a) about the end of the period` period reading calendar

@ref s.10(a) (src:110)
GIVEN period IS A `Period of a restriction or suspension under section 10`
      reading IS A `Reading of the three-year cap of section 10(a)`
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Unmet precondition of section 10`
`the unmet preconditions of section 10(a) about the end of the period` period reading calendar MEANS
    CONSIDER period's `ends on`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN LIST `the restriction or suspension has no period fixed`
    WHEN JUST end THEN
        `the unmet precondition of section 10 listed when`
            (NOT `the period ends within the three-year cap` (period's `begins on`) end reading calendar)
            `the restriction or suspension runs beyond the three years section 10(a) allows`

-- Whether the three-year cap bears on the measure on the reading: a suspension always, a restriction on the reading
-- that the cap reaches restrictions; the other measures have no period.
@ref s.10(a) (src:110)
GIVEN measure IS A `Measure under section 10(a)`
      reading IS A `Reading of the three-year cap of section 10(a)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the three-year cap bears on the measure` measure reading MEANS
    CONSIDER measure
    WHEN `refuse to renew the licence` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `make the renewal of the licence conditional on taking part in a training course under section 17` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `revoke the licence` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `restrict the licence` THEN reading's `the cap reaches restrictions`
    WHEN `suspend the licence` THEN TRUE

-- The preconditions of (a) that are not met, on a reading of the cap.  The Law's order: the Council consulted, the
-- hearing given, one of the grounds made out, and, for a restriction or suspension, a period of at most three years.
@ref s.10(a) (src:110-116)
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstances of a measure under section 10(a)`
      reading IS A `Reading of the three-year cap of section 10(a)`
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Unmet precondition of section 10`
`the preconditions of section 10(a) not met, on a reading of the cap` c reading calendar MEANS
    concat (LIST
        `the unmet precondition of section 10 listed when` (NOT (c's `the Council was consulted`)) `the Council was not consulted under section 10`
      , `the unmet precondition of section 10 listed when` ((c's `the Council was consulted`) AND NOT (c's `the Council's advice was validly given`)) `the Council's advice was not validly given under section 10`
      , `the unmet precondition of section 10 listed when` (NOT (c's `the licensee was given an opportunity to make claims in writing`)) `the licensee was not given an opportunity to make claims in writing`
      , `the unmet precondition of section 10 listed when` (NOT `a ground of section 10(a) is made out` (c's `the grounds`)) `no ground of section 10(a) is made out`
      , (IF   `the three-year cap bears on the measure` (c's `the measure`) reading
         THEN `the unmet preconditions of section 10(a) about the period` c reading calendar
         ELSE EMPTY))

@ref s.10(a) (src:110-116)
@export The preconditions of section 10(a) that are not met for the proposed measure: the Council was not consulted or its advice was not validly given, the licensee was not given an opportunity to make claims in writing, no ground is made out, or a restriction or suspension has no period or runs beyond three years; the Registrar may take the measure when the list is empty
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstances of a measure under section 10(a)` @desc The measure, the six grounds, the consultation of the Council, the written hearing and the period
GIVETH A LIST OF `Unmet precondition of section 10`
`the preconditions of section 10(a) not met` c MEANS
    `the preconditions of section 10(a) not met, on a reading of the cap` c `the reading of the cap of section 10(a) taken` `no days of rest for section 10`

@ref s.10(a) (src:110-116)
@export True if section 10(a) lets the Registrar take the proposed measure against the licence: he consulted the Council and its advice was validly given, the licensee had the opportunity to make claims in writing, one of the six grounds is made out, and a restriction or suspension is for a period of at most three years
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstances of a measure under section 10(a)` @desc The measure, the six grounds, the consultation of the Council, the written hearing and the period
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a)` c MEANS
    null (`the preconditions of section 10(a) not met` c)

-- The same power on each other reading of the cap.
@ref s.10(a) (src:110-116)
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstances of a measure under section 10(a)`
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a), the cap moving past days of rest` c calendar MEANS
    null (`the preconditions of section 10(a) not met, on a reading of the cap` c `the reading of the cap of section 10(a) moving past days of rest` calendar)

@ref s.10(a) (src:110-116)
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstances of a measure under section 10(a)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a), the cap counting the beginning day` c MEANS
    null (`the preconditions of section 10(a) not met, on a reading of the cap` c `the reading of the cap of section 10(a) counting the beginning day` `no days of rest for section 10`)

@ref s.10(a) (src:110-116)
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstances of a measure under section 10(a)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a), the cap reaching suspensions only` c MEANS
    null (`the preconditions of section 10(a) not met, on a reading of the cap` c `the reading of the cap of section 10(a) reaching suspensions only` `no days of rest for section 10`)

-- The same power where the renewal conditions of s.8 are carried into ground (2) (see above).
@ref s.10(a) (src:110-116); s.8
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstances of a measure under section 10(a)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a), the renewal conditions of section 8 carried into ground (2)` c MEANS
    IF   `a ground of section 10(a) is made out for the measure, the renewal conditions of section 8 carried into ground (2)` (c's `the grounds`) (c's `the measure`)
    THEN null (`the preconditions of section 10(a) not met` c)
    ELSE FALSE

@ref s.10(a) (src:110-116)
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstances of a measure under section 10(a)`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act of the Registrar under section 10`
`s 10(a) — the Registrar may take the measure` c MEANS
    IF   `the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a)` c
    THEN PARTY `the Registrar`
         MAY `take a measure against a licence under section 10(a)` (c's `the measure`)
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§ `s.10(b) Suspension on an indictment`

-- (b): "Without derogating from (a), the Registrar may, after consulting the Council, suspend a licence if an
-- indictment was filed against the licensee for an offence as stated in s.6(a)(3), until final judgment in the
-- matter, if he saw that the gravity of the matter or the public interest require it, and after giving the licensee
-- an opportunity to make his claims in writing."  "An offence as stated in s.6(a)(3)" is a criminal offence which,
-- by its nature, gravity or circumstances, in the Registrar's opinion makes the person unfit to be a licensee.
-- The suspension has no cap and no end date: until final judgment (P11).
-- src:117 | {{ח:תת|(ב)}} בלי לגרוע מהוראות סעיף קטן (א), הרשם רשאי, לאחר התייעצות עם המועצה, להתלות רישיון, אם הוגש נגד בעל הרישיון כתב אישום בשל ביצוע עבירה כאמור {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 6|בסעיף 6(א)(3)}}, עד למתן פסק דין סופי בעניין, והכול אם ראה שחומרת העניין או טובת הציבור מחייבות זאת ולאחר שנתן לבעל הרישיון הזדמנות לטעון את טענותיו בכתב.
@ref s.10(b) (src:117)
@desc Everything section 10(b) asks before the Registrar may suspend a licence on an indictment
DECLARE `Circumstances of a suspension under section 10(b)` HAS
    `an indictment was filed against the licensee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if an indictment was filed against the licensee
    `in the Registrar's opinion the offence makes the licensee unfit to hold a licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Registrar's opinion (section 6(a)(3)): True if the offence, by its nature, gravity or circumstances, makes the licensee unfit to be a licensee
    `the Registrar saw that the gravity of the matter or the public interest requires the suspension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Registrar's finding: True if he saw that the gravity of the matter or the public interest requires the suspension
    `the Council was consulted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the Registrar consulted the Council before suspending (IP7)
    `the Council's advice was validly given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the Council's advice was validly given (IP7)
    `the licensee was given an opportunity to make claims in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if, before the suspension, the licensee was given the opportunity to make their claims in writing

@ref s.10(b) (src:117)
@export The preconditions of section 10(b) that are not met for suspending a licence on an indictment: no indictment for an offence as stated in section 6(a)(3), no finding that the gravity of the matter or the public interest requires it, the Council not consulted or its advice not validly given, no opportunity to make claims in writing
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstances of a suspension under section 10(b)` @desc The indictment, the Registrar's opinion and finding, the consultation of the Council and the written hearing
GIVETH A LIST OF `Unmet precondition of section 10`
`the preconditions of section 10(b) not met` c MEANS
    concat (LIST
        `the unmet precondition of section 10 listed when`
            (NOT ((c's `an indictment was filed against the licensee`) AND (c's `in the Registrar's opinion the offence makes the licensee unfit to hold a licence`)))
            `no indictment was filed for an offence as stated in section 6(a)(3)`
      , `the unmet precondition of section 10 listed when` (NOT (c's `the Registrar saw that the gravity of the matter or the public interest requires the suspension`)) `the Registrar did not find that the gravity of the matter or the public interest requires the suspension`
      , `the unmet precondition of section 10 listed when` (NOT (c's `the Council was consulted`)) `the Council was not consulted under section 10`
      , `the unmet precondition of section 10 listed when` ((c's `the Council was consulted`) AND NOT (c's `the Council's advice was validly given`)) `the Council's advice was not validly given under section 10`
      , `the unmet precondition of section 10 listed when` (NOT (c's `the licensee was given an opportunity to make claims in writing`)) `the licensee was not given an opportunity to make claims in writing`)

@ref s.10(b) (src:117)
@export True if section 10(b) lets the Registrar suspend the licence until final judgment on the indictment
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstances of a suspension under section 10(b)` @desc The indictment, the Registrar's opinion and finding, the consultation of the Council and the written hearing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Registrar may suspend the licence until final judgment` c MEANS
    null (`the preconditions of section 10(b) not met` c)

@ref s.10(b) (src:117)
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstances of a suspension under section 10(b)`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act of the Registrar under section 10`
`s 10(b) — the Registrar may suspend the licence until final judgment` c MEANS
    IF   `the Registrar may suspend the licence until final judgment` c
    THEN PARTY `the Registrar`
         MAY `suspend a licence until final judgment`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- "Until final judgment" (P11, a period of validity): no number and no cap.  The suspension is in force from its
-- first day until the day of final judgment, "until" including the day (IL s.8); with no judgment yet it has no
-- end.  IL s.10(c) is not applied (a period of validity; the alternative is below).
@ref s.10(b) (src:117)
@export True if a suspension under section 10(b) is in force on the day: it began on or before the day and the day is not after the day of final judgment, if there has been one
GIVEN begins IS A DATE @desc The first day of the suspension
      `final judgment was given on` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc The day of the final judgment on the indictment; NOTHING if there has been none
      day IS A DATE @desc The day asked about
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a suspension under section 10(b) is in force on the day` begins `final judgment was given on` day MEANS
        day AT LEAST begins
    AND CONSIDER `final judgment was given on`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
        WHEN JUST judgment THEN `s 8 — the date` day `is up to and including` judgment

-- The same, "until" read as excluding the day of the judgment: the suspension ends the day before.
@ref s.10(b) (src:117)
GIVEN begins IS A DATE
      `final judgment was given on` IS A MAYBE DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a suspension under section 10(b) is in force on the day, ending before the day of the judgment` begins `final judgment was given on` day MEANS
        day AT LEAST begins
    AND CONSIDER `final judgment was given on`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
        WHEN JUST judgment THEN day LESS THAN judgment

§§ `s.10(c) A curable defect`

-- (c), first limb: "If the Registrar holds that the defect stated in (a) can be cured, he may, after consulting the
-- Council, direct that until the cure is made the licensee shall not do work on a cooling system that he specifies."
-- The text names the Council and not the written hearing for this limb.  "The defect stated in (a)" is one of the
-- six grounds.
-- src:118 | {{ח:תת|(ג)}} סבר הרשם כי הפגם כאמור בסעיף קטן (א) ניתן לתיקון, רשאי הוא, לאחר התייעצות עם המועצה, להורות כי עד לביצוע התיקון לא יבצע בעל הרישיון עבודות במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר שעליהן יורה; חלפה התקופה שקבע הרשם והפגם לא תוקן להנחת דעתו, רשאי הוא, לאחר שנתן לבעל הרישיון הזדמנות לטעון את טענותיו בכתב, לנקוט אמצעים כאמור בסעיף קטן (א).
@ref s.10(c) (src:118)
@desc Everything the first limb of section 10(c) asks before the Registrar may direct that a licensee not do specified work until a defect is cured
DECLARE `Circumstances of a direction under section 10(c)` HAS
    `the grounds` IS A `Grounds under section 10(a)` @desc The six grounds; the defect is one of them
    `the Registrar holds that the defect can be cured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Registrar's opinion: True if he holds that the defect can be cured
    `the Council was consulted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the Registrar consulted the Council before the direction (IP7)
    `the Council's advice was validly given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the Council's advice was validly given (IP7)

@ref s.10(c) (src:118)
@export The preconditions of the first limb of section 10(c) that are not met for directing that a licensee not do specified work until a defect is cured: no defect of section 10(a) is made out, the Registrar does not hold that it can be cured, the Council was not consulted or its advice was not validly given
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstances of a direction under section 10(c)` @desc The defect, the Registrar's opinion and the consultation of the Council
GIVETH A LIST OF `Unmet precondition of section 10`
`the preconditions of section 10(c) for the direction not met` c MEANS
    concat (LIST
        `the unmet precondition of section 10 listed when` (NOT `a ground of section 10(a) is made out` (c's `the grounds`)) `no ground of section 10(a) is made out`
      , `the unmet precondition of section 10 listed when` (NOT (c's `the Registrar holds that the defect can be cured`)) `the Registrar does not hold that the defect can be cured`
      , `the unmet precondition of section 10 listed when` (NOT (c's `the Council was consulted`)) `the Council was not consulted under section 10`
      , `the unmet precondition of section 10 listed when` ((c's `the Council was consulted`) AND NOT (c's `the Council's advice was validly given`)) `the Council's advice was not validly given under section 10`)

@ref s.10(c) (src:118)
@export True if the first limb of section 10(c) lets the Registrar direct that a licensee not do specified work until a defect is cured
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstances of a direction under section 10(c)` @desc The defect, the Registrar's opinion and the consultation of the Council
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Registrar may direct that the licensee not do the specified work until the defect is cured` c MEANS
    null (`the preconditions of section 10(c) for the direction not met` c)

-- The same power on the reading that the first limb needs the written hearing too (as the second limb and (a) do).
@ref s.10(c) (src:118)
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstances of a direction under section 10(c)`
      `the licensee was given an opportunity to make claims in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Registrar may direct that the licensee not do the specified work until the defect is cured, a written hearing also required` c `the licensee was given an opportunity to make claims in writing` MEANS
        `the Registrar may direct that the licensee not do the specified work until the defect is cured` c
    AND `the licensee was given an opportunity to make claims in writing`

@ref s.10(c) (src:118)
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstances of a direction under section 10(c)`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act of the Registrar under section 10`
`s 10(c) — the Registrar may direct that the licensee not do the specified work` c MEANS
    IF   `the Registrar may direct that the licensee not do the specified work until the defect is cured` c
    THEN PARTY `the Registrar`
         MAY `direct a licensee not to do specified work until a curable defect is cured`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- A restriction, suspension or bar on specified work is in force on a day: it began on or before the day and has not
-- ended; for a bar until the defect is cured, the end is the day of the cure.  This is G1's own record of what
-- limits a licensee's work; the caller sets the flag `the licensee is restricted from the work` of s.3(a) from
-- it, once it says that the restriction covers the work in question.  "Until" includes the last day (IL s.8).
@ref s.10(a) (src:110); s.10(c) (src:118)
@export True if a restriction, suspension or bar on specified work is in force on the day: it began on or before the day and its last day, if one is fixed, is not before the day
GIVEN period IS A `Period of a restriction or suspension under section 10` @desc The first day and the last day, if one is fixed; for a bar until a defect is cured, the day of the cure
      day IS A DATE @desc The day asked about
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a restriction or bar is in force on the day` period day MEANS
        day AT LEAST period's `begins on`
    AND CONSIDER period's `ends on`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
        WHEN JUST end THEN `s 8 — the date` day `is up to and including` end

-- The period the Registrar sets for the cure (P12, kind D: a deadline for doing something).  The Registrar fixes it
-- in a number of days, weeks, months or years from a day: the Law gives no length and no unit, so the length is an
-- input.  IL s.10(c) IS applied to its last day (a deadline for doing something); the alternative is below.
@desc The unit in which the Registrar fixes a period: days, weeks, months or years
DECLARE `Unit of a period fixed under section 10` IS ONE OF
    `a number of days fixed under section 10`
    `a number of weeks fixed under section 10`
    `a number of months fixed under section 10`
    `a number of years fixed under section 10`

@desc A period the Registrar fixes in a number of units from a day; the length and the unit are the Registrar's, the Law gives none
DECLARE `Period fixed by the Registrar under section 10` HAS
    `the number of units` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days, weeks, months or years
    `the unit` IS A `Unit of a period fixed under section 10` @desc Days, weeks, months or years
    `counted from the day` IS A DATE @desc The day the period is counted from: the day of the direction (section 10(c)) or of the revocation (section 10(d))

@ref s.10(a) (src:110); s.10(c) (src:118)
GIVEN p IS A `Period fixed by the Registrar under section 10`
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the period fixed by the Registrar, without IL s 10(c)` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p's `the unit`
    WHEN `a number of days fixed under section 10`   THEN `s 10(a) — the last day of a period of` (p's `the number of units`) `days from` (p's `counted from the day`)
    WHEN `a number of weeks fixed under section 10`  THEN `s 10(a) — the last day of a period of` (p's `the number of units`) `weeks from` (p's `counted from the day`)
    WHEN `a number of months fixed under section 10` THEN `s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` (p's `the number of units`) `months after an event on` (p's `counted from the day`)
    WHEN `a number of years fixed under section 10`  THEN `s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` (p's `the number of units`) `years after an event on` (p's `counted from the day`)

@ref s.10(a) (src:110); s.10(c) (src:118)
GIVEN p IS A `Period fixed by the Registrar under section 10`
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the period fixed by the Registrar, applying IL s 10(c)` p calendar MEANS
    CONSIDER p's `the unit`
    WHEN `a number of days fixed under section 10`   THEN `s 10(a), (c) — the last day of a period of` (p's `the number of units`) `days from` (p's `counted from the day`) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` (`days of rest, recess or holiday listed in` (calendar's `days of rest, recess or holiday`))
    WHEN `a number of weeks fixed under section 10`  THEN `s 10(a), (c) — the last day of a period of` (p's `the number of units`) `weeks from` (p's `counted from the day`) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` (`days of rest, recess or holiday listed in` (calendar's `days of rest, recess or holiday`))
    WHEN `a number of months fixed under section 10` THEN `s 10(b), (c) — the last day of a period of` (p's `the number of units`) `months after an event on` (p's `counted from the day`) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` (`days of rest, recess or holiday listed in` (calendar's `days of rest, recess or holiday`))
    WHEN `a number of years fixed under section 10`  THEN `s 10(b), (c) — the last day of a period of` (p's `the number of units`) `years after an event on` (p's `counted from the day`) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` (`days of rest, recess or holiday listed in` (calendar's `days of rest, recess or holiday`))

@ref s.10(c) (src:118)
@export The last day of the period the Registrar set for the cure (section 10(c)): counted from the day of the direction under IL s.10(a) and (b), and moved to the next day that is not a day of rest, recess or holiday by IL s.10(c), because it is the last day for doing something
GIVEN p IS A `Period fixed by the Registrar under section 10` @desc The length, the unit and the day of the direction
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days` @desc The days of rest, recess or holiday
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the cure period under section 10(c)` p calendar MEANS
    `the last day of the period fixed by the Registrar, applying IL s 10(c)` p calendar

@ref s.10(c) (src:118)
GIVEN p IS A `Period fixed by the Registrar under section 10`
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the cure period under section 10(c), without IL s 10(c)` p MEANS
    `the last day of the period fixed by the Registrar, without IL s 10(c)` p

-- (c), second limb: "When the period the Registrar fixed has passed and the defect was not cured to his
-- satisfaction, he may, after giving the licensee an opportunity to make his claims in writing, take measures as
-- stated in (a)."  The text names the written hearing and not the Council, and not the six grounds again (the
-- uncured defect is the ground).  Taken: the measures are (a)'s measures and the preconditions are (c)'s own words:
-- the period passed, the defect uncured to the Registrar's satisfaction, the hearing; no fresh consultation of the
-- Council.  The reading that carries (a)'s Council consultation into this limb is callable below.
@ref s.10(c) (src:118)
@desc Everything the second limb of section 10(c) asks before the Registrar may take a measure after the cure period
DECLARE `Circumstances of a measure after the cure period under section 10(c)` HAS
    `the measure under section 10(a)` IS A `Circumstances of a measure under section 10(a)` @desc The measure and the facts of section 10(a), of which the grounds, the three-year cap and, on one reading, the Council are read
    `the period the Registrar set` IS A `Period fixed by the Registrar under section 10` @desc The cure period the Registrar fixed
    `the defect was cured to the satisfaction of the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Registrar's opinion: True if the defect was cured to his satisfaction
    `the day of the measure` IS A DATE @desc The day the Registrar takes the measure

-- Whether an unmet precondition is about the Council.
@ref s.10(c) (src:118)
GIVEN item IS AN `Unmet precondition of section 10`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the unmet precondition is about the Council` item MEANS
        item EQUALS `the Council was not consulted under section 10`
    OR  item EQUALS `the Council's advice was not validly given under section 10`

-- The preconditions of the second limb, on a reading: whether IL s.10(c) moves the last day of the cure period, and
-- whether (a)'s Council consultation is carried into this limb.  The (a) preconditions are all read; the Council ones
-- are dropped when the Council is not consulted again.
@ref s.10(c) (src:118)
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstances of a measure after the cure period under section 10(c)`
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
      `IL s 10(c) is applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Council is consulted again` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Unmet precondition of section 10`
`the preconditions of section 10(c) for a measure after the cure period not met, on a reading` c calendar `IL s 10(c) is applied` `the Council is consulted again` MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (filter (GIVEN item YIELD `the Council is consulted again` OR NOT `the unmet precondition is about the Council` item)
                (`the preconditions of section 10(a) not met` (c's `the measure under section 10(a)`)))
      , `the unmet precondition of section 10 listed when`
            (NOT ((c's `the day of the measure`) GREATER THAN (`the last day of the cure period on a reading` c calendar `IL s 10(c) is applied`)))
            `the period the Registrar set has not yet passed`
      , `the unmet precondition of section 10 listed when` (c's `the defect was cured to the satisfaction of the Registrar`) `the defect was cured to the satisfaction of the Registrar, so the second limb does not arise`)

@ref s.10(c) (src:118)
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstances of a measure after the cure period under section 10(c)`
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
      `IL s 10(c) is applied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the cure period on a reading` c calendar `IL s 10(c) is applied` MEANS
    IF   `IL s 10(c) is applied`
    THEN `the last day of the cure period under section 10(c)` (c's `the period the Registrar set`) calendar
    ELSE `the last day of the cure period under section 10(c), without IL s 10(c)` (c's `the period the Registrar set`)

@ref s.10(c) (src:118)
@export The preconditions of the second limb of section 10(c) that are not met for taking a measure after the cure period: the period the Registrar set (its last day moved by IL s.10(c)) has not passed, the defect was cured to his satisfaction, the licensee was not given the opportunity to make claims in writing, no ground is made out; the Council is not asked again
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstances of a measure after the cure period under section 10(c)` @desc The measure, the cure period, the Registrar's opinion and the day of the measure
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days` @desc The days of rest, recess or holiday
GIVETH A LIST OF `Unmet precondition of section 10`
`the preconditions of section 10(c) for a measure after the cure period not met` c calendar MEANS
    `the preconditions of section 10(c) for a measure after the cure period not met, on a reading` c calendar TRUE FALSE

@ref s.10(c) (src:118)
@export True if the second limb of section 10(c) lets the Registrar take a measure of section 10(a) after the cure period
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstances of a measure after the cure period under section 10(c)` @desc The measure, the cure period, the Registrar's opinion and the day of the measure
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days` @desc The days of rest, recess or holiday
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Registrar may take the measure after the cure period` c calendar MEANS
    null (`the preconditions of section 10(c) for a measure after the cure period not met` c calendar)

-- The second limb on the reading that carries (a)'s Council consultation into it.
@ref s.10(c) (src:118)
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstances of a measure after the cure period under section 10(c)`
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Registrar may take the measure after the cure period, the Council consulted again` c calendar MEANS
    null (`the preconditions of section 10(c) for a measure after the cure period not met, on a reading` c calendar TRUE TRUE)

-- The second limb with the cure period counted without IL s.10(c): it ends on its nominal last day even when that is
-- a day of rest.
@ref s.10(c) (src:118)
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstances of a measure after the cure period under section 10(c)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Registrar may take the measure after the cure period, without IL s 10(c)` c MEANS
    null (`the preconditions of section 10(c) for a measure after the cure period not met, on a reading` c `no days of rest for section 10` FALSE FALSE)

@ref s.10(c) (src:118)
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstances of a measure after the cure period under section 10(c)`
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act of the Registrar under section 10`
`s 10(c) — the Registrar may take the measure after the cure period` c calendar MEANS
    IF   `the Registrar may take the measure after the cure period` c calendar
    THEN PARTY `the Registrar`
         MAY `take a measure against a licence under section 10(a)` ((c's `the measure under section 10(a)`)'s `the measure`)
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§ `s.10(d) The bar after a revocation`

-- (d): "Where a licence was revoked under (a), the Registrar shall, after consulting the Council and according to the
-- circumstances of the case, direct the period of time only after which that person may submit a new application for
-- a licence, and the Registrar may make the grant of a new licence to that person conditional on conditions additional
-- to those listed in ss.6 or 9, as the case may be, including additional training requirements."
-- The direction is a duty ("shall direct"), with no deadline stated.  The additional conditions are a power
-- ("may"); the consultation is named in the first clause only, so the power is taken to need only the revocation (a fork;
-- the reading that it needs the consultation too is below).  The length of the bar is the Registrar's: an input, with no
-- default (P13, kind W: a window for an application).  IL s.10(c) is applied to the last day of the bar.
-- src:119 | {{ח:תת|(ד)}} בוטל רישיון לפי סעיף קטן (א), יורה הרשם, לאחר התייעצות עם המועצה ובהתאם לנסיבות המקרה, על פרק הזמן שרק לאחריו יהיה אותו אדם רשאי להגיש בקשה חדשה לרישיון, ורשאי הרשם להתנות מתן רישיון חדש לאותו אדם בתנאים נוספים על אלה המנויים {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 6|בסעיפים 6}} {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 9|או 9}}, לפי העניין, לרבות דרישות הכשרה נוספות.
@ref s.10(d) (src:119)
@desc Everything section 10(d) asks before the Registrar must direct the period before a new application may be made
DECLARE `Circumstances of a bar after revocation under section 10(d)` HAS
    `the licence was revoked under section 10(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the licence was revoked under section 10(a)
    `the Council was consulted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the Registrar consulted the Council before directing the period (IP7)
    `the Council's advice was validly given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the Council's advice was validly given (IP7)

@ref s.10(d) (src:119)
@export The preconditions of section 10(d) that are not met for directing the period before a new application may be made: the licence was not revoked under section 10(a), the Council was not consulted or its advice was not validly given
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstances of a bar after revocation under section 10(d)` @desc The revocation and the consultation of the Council
GIVETH A LIST OF `Unmet precondition of section 10`
`the preconditions of section 10(d) for the bar not met` c MEANS
    concat (LIST
        `the unmet precondition of section 10 listed when` (NOT (c's `the licence was revoked under section 10(a)`)) `the licence was not revoked under section 10(a)`
      , `the unmet precondition of section 10 listed when` (NOT (c's `the Council was consulted`)) `the Council was not consulted under section 10`
      , `the unmet precondition of section 10 listed when` ((c's `the Council was consulted`) AND NOT (c's `the Council's advice was validly given`)) `the Council's advice was not validly given under section 10`)

@ref s.10(d) (src:119)
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstances of a bar after revocation under section 10(d)`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act of the Registrar under section 10`
`s 10(d) — the Registrar must direct the period before a new application may be made` c MEANS
    IF   null (`the preconditions of section 10(d) for the bar not met` c)
    THEN PARTY `the Registrar`
         MUST `fix the period before a new application may be made after a revocation`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY `the Registrar`
               BECAUSE "section 10(d): the Registrar did not direct the period before which the person may not submit a new application"
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref s.10(d) (src:119)
@export True if section 10(d) lets the Registrar make the grant of a new licence conditional on additional conditions, including additional training: the licence was revoked under section 10(a)
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstances of a bar after revocation under section 10(d)` @desc The revocation and the consultation of the Council
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Registrar may add conditions to the grant of a new licence` c MEANS
    c's `the licence was revoked under section 10(a)`

-- The same power on the reading that it needs the Council's consultation too.
@ref s.10(d) (src:119)
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstances of a bar after revocation under section 10(d)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Registrar may add conditions to the grant of a new licence, the Council consulted` c MEANS
    null (`the preconditions of section 10(d) for the bar not met` c)

@ref s.10(d) (src:119)
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstances of a bar after revocation under section 10(d)`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act of the Registrar under section 10`
`s 10(d) — the Registrar may add conditions to the grant of a new licence` c MEANS
    IF   `the Registrar may add conditions to the grant of a new licence` c
    THEN PARTY `the Registrar`
         MAY `add conditions to the grant of a new licence`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- The last day of the bar (P13, kind W): IL s.10(c) IS applied, so a bar whose last day is a day of rest ends on the
-- next day that is not one; the alternative without IL s.10(c) is below.  The person may submit a new application
-- only AFTER the last day of the bar, a comparison and not an addition to a date.
@ref s.10(d) (src:119)
@export The last day of the bar the Registrar directed after a revocation (section 10(d)): counted from the day of the revocation under IL s.10(a) and (b), and moved to the next day that is not a day of rest, recess or holiday by IL s.10(c), because the window for a new application opens only after it
GIVEN p IS A `Period fixed by the Registrar under section 10` @desc The length, the unit and the day of the revocation
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days` @desc The days of rest, recess or holiday
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the bar under section 10(d)` p calendar MEANS
    `the last day of the period fixed by the Registrar, applying IL s 10(c)` p calendar

@ref s.10(d) (src:119)
GIVEN p IS A `Period fixed by the Registrar under section 10`
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the bar under section 10(d), without IL s 10(c)` p MEANS
    `the last day of the period fixed by the Registrar, without IL s 10(c)` p

@ref s.10(d) (src:119)
@export True if a new application may be made on the day after a revocation: the day is after the last day of the bar the Registrar directed, counted with IL s.10(c)
GIVEN p IS A `Period fixed by the Registrar under section 10` @desc The length, the unit and the day of the revocation
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days` @desc The days of rest, recess or holiday
      day IS A DATE @desc The day of the new application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a new application may be made on the day after the bar` p calendar day MEANS
    day GREATER THAN (`the last day of the bar under section 10(d)` p calendar)

@ref s.10(d) (src:119)
GIVEN p IS A `Period fixed by the Registrar under section 10`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a new application may be made on the day after the bar, without IL s 10(c)` p day MEANS
    day GREATER THAN (`the last day of the bar under section 10(d), without IL s 10(c)` p)

-- The additional conditions of (d): further training (IP6: the Registrar's requirement is an input) and any other
-- condition he fixed.
@ref s.10(d) (src:119)
@desc The additional conditions the Registrar fixed for a new licence under section 10(d)
DECLARE `Additional conditions under section 10(d)` HAS
    `further training the Registrar required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the Registrar required additional training before a new licence is granted
    `the further training was completed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the person completed the further training the Registrar required
    `the other additional conditions the Registrar fixed were met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if every other additional condition the Registrar fixed was met; True if he fixed none

@ref s.10(d) (src:119)
@export True if the additional conditions the Registrar fixed for a new licence under section 10(d) are met: the further training he required, if any, was completed, and every other condition was met
GIVEN conditions IS AN `Additional conditions under section 10(d)` @desc The further training and any other conditions the Registrar fixed
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the additional conditions of section 10(d) are met` conditions MEANS
        (   NOT conditions's `further training the Registrar required`
         OR conditions's `the further training was completed`)
    AND conditions's `the other additional conditions the Registrar fixed were met`

§§ `s.10 The effect of revocation and suspension on whether a licence is in force`

-- Revocation and suspension under s.10 take a licence out of force.  The domain Licence records the day of a revocation
-- and the first and last day of a suspension.  The Law names no effective day for a revocation: the day the register
-- records is taken as the first day without the licence (a fork).  A suspension runs from its first day to its last
-- day, "until" including the day (IL s.8); with no last day it runs on (a suspension until final judgment).
-- The licence's validity under ss.8 and 9 is G2's rule (IP1).
@ref s.10(a) (src:110); s.10(b) (src:117)
@export True if the licence was revoked under section 10 on or before the day
GIVEN licence IS A Licence @desc The licence as the register records it
      day IS A DATE @desc The day asked about
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 10 — the licence is revoked on the day` licence day MEANS
    CONSIDER licence's `revoked on`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST revoked THEN day AT LEAST revoked

-- The same, the revocation taking effect the day AFTER the day the register records.
@ref s.10(a) (src:110)
GIVEN licence IS A Licence
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 10 — the licence is revoked on the day, the revocation taking effect the day after the day recorded` licence day MEANS
    CONSIDER licence's `revoked on`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST revoked THEN day GREATER THAN revoked

@ref s.10(a) (src:110); s.10(b) (src:117)
@export True if the licence is under a suspension of section 10 on the day: the suspension began on or before the day and its last day, if one is fixed, is not before the day
GIVEN licence IS A Licence @desc The licence as the register records it
      day IS A DATE @desc The day asked about
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 10 — the licence is suspended on the day` licence day MEANS
    CONSIDER licence's `suspended from`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST first THEN
            day AT LEAST first
        AND CONSIDER licence's `suspended until`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
            WHEN JUST last THEN `s 8 — the date` day `is up to and including` last

@ref s.10(a) (src:110); s.10(b) (src:117)
@export True if section 10 takes the licence out of force on the day: it was revoked on or before the day, or it is under a suspension on the day
GIVEN licence IS A Licence @desc The licence as the register records it
      day IS A DATE @desc The day asked about
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 10 — the licence is out of force by reason of section 10 on the day` licence day MEANS
        `s 10 — the licence is revoked on the day` licence day
    OR  `s 10 — the licence is suspended on the day` licence day
